Open Vanilla 0054: Boss Fights bot fill. A raid nobody else joins is filled with bots: when the oldest ticket of a
pool has waited OpenVanilla.BossFights.BotFill.After (30 s), it takes the younger people of its pool who fit and
asks for bots for the seats left, by role (the missing tanks: Warriors; healers: Priest, Druid, Paladin or
Shaman; then damage), of the leader's faction, at level 60 with the bot factory's epic gear and their role's
talents. They are characters on the bot AI's accounts (RNDBOT*), kept in bossfights_fill_bot and made the first
time a role, class and faction is needed; they log in at the hangout (no raid save of an old run), join the
ticket when ready, and it pops whole. In the run they follow and fight with the group's person as master, the
dungeon strategies on. They log out as soon as nothing wants them: the ticket is gone, the run is over or left,
or none of its people has been online for a minute (a run with bots then ends). Limits: .BotFill.Max (18 logged
in, realm-wide; a fill must fit whole) and .BotFill.MinFreeMB (600: the host's MemAvailable and the room under
the container's limit). The waiting line gains ,<state>,<seconds>,<ready>,<wanted> where bots may fill it (state:
wait, joining, ready, full, off, ai, memory, max, error); the hello is followed by fill,<1|0>,<after>; bots are never
counted as players (live counts, bossfights_now.size); runs with bots rank on their own boards as before.
Self-test: "q <raid> size=<n> bots=1" fills at once; "test state" adds bots, botsin, fillalive, fill.
Needs AiPlayerbot.Enabled = 1 (no random bots: RandomBotAutologin 0, Min/MaxRandomBots 0) and the bot AI's
tables (hetzner/bossfights_up.sh botfill on).

