+ * Bot fill (realm/mangos/0054; on with OpenVanilla.BossFights = 1 and the bot AI, AiPlayerbot.Enabled = 1):
+ *   OpenVanilla.BossFights.BotFill            1     bots fill the seats nobody else takes
+ *   OpenVanilla.BossFights.BotFill.After      30    seconds the oldest ticket of a pool waits before bots come (0: at once)
+ *   OpenVanilla.BossFights.BotFill.Max        18    most fill bots logged in at once, realm-wide (a raid's whole fill
+ *                                                   must fit, or it waits)
+ *   OpenVanilla.BossFights.BotFill.MinFreeMB  600   no new bots below this much free memory (the host's MemAvailable,
+ *                                                   and what is left under the container's limit)
+ * When its turn comes, a ticket takes the younger people of its pool who fit, then asks for bots for the seats
+ * left: the missing tanks (Warriors), healers (Priest, Druid, Paladin or Shaman) and damage, of the leader's
+ * faction, level 60 with the bot factory's epic gear and their role's talents. They are characters on the bot AI's
+ * accounts (RNDBOT*), kept in bossfights_fill_bot and made the first time a role and class is needed; they log in
+ * at the hangout, join the ticket when ready, and the ticket pops whole. In the run they follow and fight with the
+ * group's person as master (the dungeon strategies on). They log out as soon as nothing wants them: the ticket is
+ * gone, the run is over or left, or (a run with bots) none of its people has been online for a minute. Bots are
+ * never counted as players (the live counts, bossfights_now.size), and a run with bots ranks on its own boards.
+ * The waiting line gains four fields where bots may fill it: ,<state>,<seconds>,<ready>,<wanted> with the state
+ *   wait (bots come in <seconds>) | joining (<ready> of <wanted> in) | ready (all in: it pops) | full (people fill it)
+ *   | off | ai | memory | max | error (bots can't come now: it waits for people)
+ * and the hello is followed by  fill,<1|0>,<after seconds>.  Self-test: "q <raid> size=<n> bots=1" fills at once;
